NOT COVERED BY THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE

The MIT license covers the code. The following files are NOT covered by it.

1. Zeke & Learn brand assets and character art: Copyright (c) 2026 Zeke Espirito
   Sebulino (Zeke & Learn). All rights reserved.

   - app/assets/brand/   The Zeke & Learn logo mark, wordmark and icons.
   - app/assets/guide/   The "Cap Zeke" guide character art.
   - docs/               The pixel Zeke character in docs and demo renders.
   - app/assets/sample/  The sample voice: an AI clone of Zeke's voice, made
                         with ElevenLabs, and its timing data.

   You may not use these as a presenter, mascot, logo, avatar, voice or
   training data, or in your own products. They are included only so this
   project's own copy of the app works out of the box. If you fork this
   repository and host or distribute your own copy, replace them with your own.

2. Fonts in app/assets/fonts/ (Space Grotesk, JetBrains Mono, Silkscreen) are
   licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Their license files are next to
   them (OFL-*.txt). The engine installs Space Grotesk, JetBrains Mono and
   Pixelify Sans from npm, also under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

3. Third-party code bundled in app/vendor/ (mp4-muxer, webm-muxer) is under
   the MIT license with its own copyright notices (LICENSE-* files in that
   folder).

4. Speech models are not bundled. Sharper lip sync and the `listen` command
   download them at runtime from Hugging Face, each under its own license
   (see README.md, Credits).

Pixel icons and synthesized sounds in engine/ are original to Mascot Booth and
are covered by the MIT license above.
